Fri Nov 20 17:43:14 UTC 2026 - Fridrich Strba <fstrba@suse.com>

- Upgrade to version 5.6.5
  * Changes
    + Fixed async Brotli decompression hang with large input buffers
    + HTTPCLIENT-2433: prevent concurrent HTTP/2 request body replay
    + HTTPCLIENT-2432: fixed connection-pool leak in
      ResponseEntityProxy#cleanup() when #disconnectEndpoint throws
    + Decode punycode public suffixes in PublicSuffixMatcher#verify
    + HTTP cache: treat malformed delta-seconds as absent, fix
      neverCache1_1ResponsesWithQueryString handling, remove invalid
      request version check, fix resource leak on error in
      AsyncCachingExec

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Aug 13 12:00:00 UTC 2026 - Fridrich Strba <fstrba@suse.com>

- Upgrade to version 5.6.4:
  * Release 5.6.4
    + SSL Parameter Fix: This maintenance release fixes SSL parameter
      application in the async TLS upgrade strategy
    + BearerScheme to reject control characters in bearer token
  * Release 5.6.3
    + Fixes a resource management defect in the content decompression
      protocol handler of the classic transport
    + ContentCompressionExec fails to close the underlying response
      stream in case of an unexpected runtime or protocol exception
      (bsc#1273163, CVE-2026-64607)
    + Do not call the backend when an only-if-cached request cannot
      be served from cache (RFC 9111 5.2.1.7)
    + Include the request scheme in redirect same-authority check
    + Escape quotes and strip line breaks in RFC 7578 multipart
      parameters
    + HTTPCLIENT-2426: Do not wrap a discarded (null) response body
      in a content decoder
  * Release 5.6.2
    + Upgraded HttpCore to version 5.4.3
    + HTTPCLIENT-2422: Restore lazy content decompression. Defer
      construction of the decompression stream until the response
      content is actually read
  * Release 5.6.1
    + Disables experimental SCRAM auth scheme by default and fixes
      SCRAM final response handling
    + Fix SCRAM final response handling
    + Auth challenge parsing code improvement
    + Corrected async message exchange cancellation logic in
      InternalHttpAsyncExecRuntime
    + HTTPCLIENT-2417: Honor TlsConfig attachment in async connect path
    + HTTPCLIENT-2414: Fix Basic auth cache scoping across path prefixes
    + HTTPCLIENT-2415: Normalize CookieOrigin path for cookie matching
    + DefaultManagedHttpClientConnection: Restore original socket timeout
  * Release 5.6.0
    + Adds several features such as transport content decompression and
      content compression for the async transport, support for Unix sockets,
      experimental support for SCRAM-SHA-256 authentication scheme, and
      Micrometer/OTel observations & metrics
    + Unix domain socket support
    + Support for pluggable content codecs via Commons-Compress in the
      classic transport
    + Support for transparent content decompression and content compression
      with deflate, gzip, zstd, and brotli codecs in the async transport
    + Micrometer/OTel observations & metrics
    + Off-lock connection disposal by the classic pooling connection
      manager
    + SCRAM-SHA-256 authentication scheme (RFC 7804)
    + Request Priority support (RFC 9218)
    + OFFLOCK connection pool concurrency policy
    + Five-second TCP keep-alive is now enabled by default
  * Release 5.5.0
    + Improved conformance to RFC 7616 (HTTP Digest Access Authentication)
    + The connection pool implementation acts as a caching facade in
      front of a standard managed connection pool and shares already
      leased connections to multiplex message exchanges over active
      HTTP/2 connections
    + Extended Auth API and improved authentication protocol logic to
      support mutual authentication
    + The Classic API facade now acts as a compatibility bridge between
      the classic I/O client services and the asynchronous message transport
- Rediff patch:
  * httpcomponents-client5-conscrypt.patch

